    "q-213227": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213227",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14268138/assets/26fe3edb60b89e021cb7fbb0660e92bc2d8199508e2c55180ff54fc34b87b084.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A=\\{a,b,c\\}?$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(a,a)\\notin R,\\,(b,b)\\notin R,\\,(c,c)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14268138/assets/f8895e2787c1bf5a0191019f7583e414311d7df9d3dd08e2036d01173abd0579.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
