    "q-213203": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213203",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nThe relation $R$ is reflexive. Indeed, since $x≡x\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ for all $x\\in Z,$ we have $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in Z,$ the relation is $\\text{reflexive }.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-213203-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "0",
              "dom_id": null,
